<title>PORTUGAL: Price dips on Portugal 7-yr, variable rate bonds.</title>
<headline>Price dips on Portugal 7-yr, variable rate bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Portuguese Institute for Public Credit Management auction of 25 billion escudos of seven-year variable-rate bonds (OTRV)</p>
<p>    ISSUER: Republic of Portugal   MATURITY:30/7/2004</p>
<p>AMOUNT PLACED: Five billion escudos</p>
<p>AVERAGE ACCEPTED PRICE: 99.3230</p>
<p>HIGHEST ACCEPTED: 99.35 LOWEST: 99.31</p>
<p>INTEREST: Indexed to six-month Lisbor less 25 basis points</p>
<p>PAYMENT DATE: 26/8/97  BIDS: 28.75 billion escuduos</p>
<p>PAYMENT FREQUENCY: Six months</p>
<p>NOTES: The price compares with 99.35 at the previous issue. The bonds are fungible and bring the total amounted issued to 102.87 billion escudos.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
